> It might be cleaner if we have something like:
> 
> struct bt_le_peer {
u8_t id;
bt_addr_le_t *addr;
}

There are further issues with `bt_gatt_clear`, `bt_gatt_clear_ccc` and `find_sc_cfg`  checked the `id` (cf_cfg and remove_subscription did not). So I find myself reconsidering this suggestion. There is already a struct similar to what you suggest, named `struct addr_with_id`. However `struct bt_gatt_ccc_cfg` is declared in public `gatt.h` header file.  
Is it acceptable to change this definition?
It's only use is by `struct _bt_gatt_ccc`, which is marked as internal representation of CCC value.
